{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/jing/file.cljc | sed -n '90,155p;265,465p'\"","aggregated_output":"    90\t\n    91\t;; =============================================================================\n    92\t;; Frame codec: [digest payload-bytes] as one canonical CBOR array\n    93\t;; =============================================================================\n    94\t\n    95\t(def ^:private max-frame-length\n    96\t  \"The largest frame the signed 32-bit length prefix can describe.\"\n    97\t  2147483647)\n    98\t\n    99\t\n   100\t(defn- frame-bytes\n   101\t  \"The frame (without its length prefix) carrying payload bytes at address.\"\n   102\t  [address payload-bytes]\n   103\t  (let [frame (cbor/encode [(hex->bytes (jing/segment-digest address))\n   104\t                            payload-bytes])]\n   105\t    (when (> (byte-count frame) max-frame-length)\n   106\t      (throw (ex-info \"Frame exceeds the length prefix's positive range\"\n   107\t                      {:address address, :length (byte-count frame)})))\n   108\t    frame))\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\t(defn encode-record\n   112\t  \"Encode an [address payload] pair into frame bytes (the length prefix is\n   113\t   written by the frame layer). The payload must hash to the address.\"\n   114\t  [address payload]\n   115\t  (frame-bytes address (jing/segment-bytes address payload)))\n   116\t\n   117\t\n   118\t(defn- decode-frame\n   119\t  \"[address payload-bytes] of one frame: the frame must be exactly one\n   120\t   canonical two-element CBOR array of byte strings, the digest must be\n   121\t   the payload's under some registered algorithm (which then names the\n   122\t   address), and the payload must itself be a canonical Jing payload.\"\n   123\t  [frame]\n   124\t  (let [v (try (cbor/decode frame)\n   125\t               (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   126\t                 (throw (ex-info \"Frame is not a canonical CBOR record\"\n   127\t                                 {:frame frame} e))))]\n   128\t    (when-not (and (vector? v) (= 2 (count v))\n   129\t                   (every? cbor/byte-payload? v))\n   130\t      (throw (ex-info \"Frame is not a [digest payload] array of byte strings\"\n   131\t                      {:record v})))\n   132\t    (let [[digest payload] v\n   133\t          hex (bytes->hex digest)\n   134\t          address-id\n   135\t          (some (fn [[algorithm {:keys [address-id digest-bytes]}]]\n   136\t                  (when (and (= digest-bytes (byte-count digest))\n   137\t                             (= hex (jing/digest-bytes algorithm payload)))\n   138\t                    address-id))\n   139\t                (sort-by key jing/registry))]\n   140\t      (when-not address-id\n   141\t        (throw (ex-info\n   142\t                 (str \"Frame digest is not the payload's under any \"\n   143\t                      \"registered algorithm\")\n   144\t                 {:digest hex})))\n   145\t      (try (cbor/decode payload)\n   146\t           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   147\t             (throw (ex-info \"Frame payload is not a canonical Jing payload\"\n   148\t                             {:digest hex} e))))\n   149\t      [(keyword \"segment\" (str address-id \"-\" hex)) payload])))\n   150\t\n   151\t\n   152\t;; =============================================================================\n   153\t;; Host file primitives -- the only host-aware code below\n   154\t;; =============================================================================\n   155\t\n   265\t\n   266\t(defn- torn-tail-offset\n   267\t  \"The offset of the first incomplete frame, scanning from 0: a tail shorter\n   268\t   than the length prefix, a negative length, or a length reaching past\n   269\t   `end` is torn. Returns `end` when every frame is complete.\"\n   270\t  [f end]\n   271\t  (loop [offset 0]\n   272\t    (cond\n   273\t      (>= offset end) end\n   274\t      (< (- end offset) prefix-size) offset\n   275\t      :else (let [len (read-int! f offset)]\n   276\t              (if (or (neg? len) (> (+ offset prefix-size len) end))\n   277\t                offset\n   278\t                (recur (+ offset prefix-size len)))))))\n   279\t\n   280\t\n   281\t(defn- recover!\n   282\t  \"Every complete frame of the file, decoded and validated in order as\n   283\t   [address payload-bytes], with the incomplete tail truncated afterwards.\n   284\t   Validation precedes mutation: a corrupt complete frame, or a nonempty\n   285\t   file with no valid first frame, throws with the file untouched.\"\n   286\t  [f]\n   287\t  (let [end (file-length! f)\n   288\t        cut (torn-tail-offset f end)\n   289\t        records (loop [offset 0, acc []]\n   290\t                  (if (>= offset cut)\n   291\t                    acc\n   292\t                    (let [len (read-int! f offset)]\n   293\t                      (recur (+ offset prefix-size len)\n   294\t                             (conj acc\n   295\t                                   (decode-frame\n   296\t                                     (read-bytes! f (+ offset prefix-size)\n   297\t                                                  len)))))))]\n   298\t    (when (and (pos? end) (empty? records))\n   299\t      (throw (ex-info \"Not a content log: no valid first frame\"\n   300\t                      {:length end})))\n   301\t    (when (< cut end) (truncate-file! f cut))\n   302\t    records))\n   303\t\n   304\t\n   305\t(defn- replay-records\n   306\t  \"Accumulate validated records into the content map. An equal duplicate\n   307\t   record is tolerated (F2), which requires comparing the incoming bytes\n   308\t   with the stored ones; the unequal arm of that comparison fails the open.\n   309\t\n   310\t   That arm is unreachable twice over: decode-frame has already enforced\n   311\t   that a frame's digest hashes its payload, so two validated frames at one\n   312\t   address carry equal bytes; and reaching it otherwise would take a hash\n   313\t   collision, which is not a case to design for. It is retained not as\n   314\t   defence but because F2's tolerate-equal rule forces the comparison, and\n   315\t   the only alternatives to throwing here are to overwrite silently or to\n   316\t   ignore silently -- both of which break `materialize!`'s promise that\n   317\t   nothing is ever overwritten.\"\n   318\t  [records]\n   319\t  (reduce (fn [content [address payload]]\n   320\t            (if (contains? content address)\n   321\t              (if (cbor/bytes= (clojure.core/get content address) payload)\n   322\t                content\n   323\t                (throw (ex-info\n   324\t                         \"Collision: address already holds a different payload\"\n   325\t                         {:address address})))\n   326\t              (assoc content address payload)))\n   327\t          {}\n   328\t          records))\n   329\t\n   330\t\n   331\t;; =============================================================================\n   332\t;; Handle functions (D1, D3, F1)\n   333\t;; =============================================================================\n   334\t\n   335\t(defn- with-lock\n   336\t  #_{:clj-kondo/ignore [:unused-binding]}\n   337\t  [lock f]\n   338\t  #?(:clj (locking lock (f))\n   339\t     :default (f)))\n   340\t\n   341\t\n   342\t(defn- make-put\n   343\t  [state f lock]\n   344\t  (fn content-put!\n   345\t    [address bs]\n   346\t    (when-not (jing/segment-address? address)\n   347\t      (throw (ex-info \"Not a segment content address\" {:address address})))\n   348\t    (when-not (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bs)\n   349\t      (throw (ex-info \"Segment address does not match the bytes\"\n   350\t                      {:address address})))\n   351\t    (let [snapshot (cbor/copy-bytes bs)\n   352\t          frame (frame-bytes address snapshot)]\n   353\t      (with-lock\n   354\t        lock\n   355\t        (fn []\n   356\t          (let [{:keys [closed? content]} @state]\n   357\t            (when closed?\n   358\t              (throw (ex-info \"Content file is closed\" {:address address})))\n   359\t            (if (contains? content address)\n   360\t              (if (cbor/bytes= (clojure.core/get content address) bs)\n   361\t                :present\n   362\t                (throw (ex-info\n   363\t                         \"Collision: address already holds a different payload\"\n   364\t                         {:address address})))\n   365\t              (do\n   366\t                (append-frame! f frame)\n   367\t                (sync-file! f)\n   368\t                (swap! state assoc-in [:content address] snapshot)\n   369\t                :inserted))))))))\n   370\t\n   371\t\n   372\t(defn- make-get\n   373\t  [state]\n   374\t  (fn content-get\n   375\t    [address not-found]\n   376\t    (let [{:keys [closed? content]} @state]\n   377\t      (when closed?\n   378\t        (throw (ex-info \"Content file is closed\" {:address address})))\n   379\t      (if (contains? content address)\n   380\t        (cbor/copy-bytes (clojure.core/get content address))\n   381\t        not-found))))\n   382\t\n   383\t\n   384\t(defn- make-close\n   385\t  [state f lock]\n   386\t  (fn content-close!\n   387\t    []\n   388\t    (with-lock\n   389\t      lock\n   390\t      (fn []\n   391\t        (when-not (:closed? @state)\n   392\t          (swap! state assoc :closed? true)\n   393\t          (close-file! f))\n   394\t        nil))))\n   395\t\n   396\t\n   397\t;; =============================================================================\n   398\t;; Constructor\n   399\t;; =============================================================================\n   400\t\n   401\t(defn create-content-file\n   402\t  \"Open or create a content file at path: validate every complete frame,\n   403\t   truncate any incomplete tail (F3), replay every record into an\n   404\t   in-memory map of address to payload bytes (F2, F4), and return the\n   405\t   plain-data byte-store handle {:put-bytes-fn :get-bytes-fn :close-fn}\n   406\t   (D1). A\n   407\t   frame that is not a canonical [digest payload] record, whose digest is\n   408\t   not its payload's under a registered algorithm, or whose payload is not\n   409\t   canonical fails the open, loudly and without mutation (F4).\"\n   410\t  [path]\n   411\t  (let [f (open-file! path)]\n   412\t    (try (let [recovered (replay-records (recover! f))\n   413\t               state (atom {:closed? false, :content recovered})\n   414\t               lock #?(:clj (Object.)\n   415\t                       :cljs (js-obj)\n   416\t                       :cljd (Object.))]\n   417\t           {:put-bytes-fn (make-put state f lock),\n   418\t            :get-bytes-fn (make-get state),\n   419\t            :close-fn (make-close state f lock)})\n   420\t         (catch #?(:clj Exception\n   421\t                   :cljs :default\n   422\t                   :cljd Object)\n   423\t                e\n   424\t           (try (close-file! f)\n   425\t                (catch #?(:clj Exception\n   426\t                          :cljs :default\n   427\t                          :cljd Object)\n   428\t                       _\n   429\t                  nil))\n   430\t           (throw e)))))\n   431\t\n   432\t\n   433\t;; =============================================================================\n   434\t;; The test's view of a path (F5)\n   435\t;; =============================================================================\n   436\t\n   437\t(defn records\n   438\t  \"The decoded, validated [address value] record vector of the file at\n   439\t   path -- every frame in order, equal duplicates included. Opens with the\n   440\t   same validate-then-truncate pass as create-content-file, reads and\n   441\t   closes. This is the file backend's test-facing view (D4): what the\n   442\t   in-memory map holds is observable through the handle; what the file\n   443\t   holds is observable here.\"\n   444\t  [path]\n   445\t  (let [f (open-file! path)]\n   446\t    (try (mapv (fn [[address payload]]\n   447\t                 [address (jing/segment-value address payload)])\n   448\t               (recover! f))\n   449\t         (finally (close-file! f)))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
