{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/dao.jing.hash-registry.md | sed -n '112,142p;492,512p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/jing/mem.cljc | sed -n '26,160p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/jing/file.cljc | sed -n '94,158p;260,385p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc | sed -n '284,312p;1160,1183p'; nl -ba test/yin/vm/pipeline_test.cljc | sed -n '485,517p;567,595p'; nl -ba docs/design/dao.jing.md | sed -n '527,543p'\"","aggregated_output":"   112\t(sha256 s)\n   113\t(sha256-bytes bytes)\n   114\t(blake3 s)\n   115\t(blake3-bytes bytes)\n   116\t```\n   117\t\n   118\tThese functions never follow the default. `sha256` remains useful to VM and DHT contracts independently of its membership in the DaoJing address registry.\n   119\t\n   120\t### `canonical-bytes`\n   121\t\n   122\tThe signature remains:\n   123\t\n   124\t```clojure\n   125\t(canonical-bytes value)\n   126\t```\n   127\t\n   128\tIt continues to return the UTF-8 bytes of the current order-normalized, metadata-aware print encoding.\n   129\t\n   130\tNo algorithm-specific canonicalization is permitted. BLAKE3 and SHA-256 receive identical bytes for the same value.\n   131\t\n   132\tThe future CBOR epic will replace this implementation outright. It will not add a second coexisting encoder or alter this function's public role.\n   133\t\n   134\t### `content-hash`\n   135\t\n   136\tRetain:\n   137\t\n   138\t```clojure\n   139\t(content-hash value)\n   140\t```\n   141\t\n   142\tIt hashes `canonical-bytes` with BLAKE3.\n   492\t- chunk and tree-boundary vectors;\n   493\t- a cross-host fixture corpus;\n   494\t- isolation behind `digest-bytes`; and\n   495\t- a provider-replacement procedure that requires complete conformance before adoption.\n   496\t\n   497\tThe Dart dependency is pure Dart and passed official vectors, but has only one release and a short history. It receives the same fixture and replacement discipline. It is also the Dart host's first external cryptographic dependency, so dependency resolution and release-build execution are explicit gates.\n   498\t\n   499\t`@noble/hashes` is actively maintained, but its ESM/package integration must be exercised in the current Shadow-CLJS test and optimized-release builds.\n   500\t\n   501\tAny provider version or replacement that changes a pinned digest is rejected as nonconforming to the registered algorithm.\n   502\t\n   503\t## Sequencing with canonical CBOR\n   504\t\n   505\tThe algorithm-registry epic lands first over the current order-normalized print encoder.\n   506\t\n   507\tIt establishes:\n   508\t\n   509\t- the flat multihash address grammar;\n   510\t- permanent BLAKE3 and SHA-256 entries;\n   511\t- BLAKE3 as the minting default;\n   512\t- explicit SHA-256 minting;\n    26\t   after close throw; close itself is idempotent.\"\n    27\t  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n    28\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]))\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\t(defn- validate-address-bytes!\n    32\t  \"Reject a put before any write: the address must be a valid segment\n    33\t   content address whose digest is the hash of exactly these bytes.\"\n    34\t  [address bs]\n    35\t  (when-not (jing/segment-address? address)\n    36\t    (throw (ex-info \"dao.jing.mem: not a segment content address\"\n    37\t                    {:address address})))\n    38\t  (when-not (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bs)\n    39\t    (throw (ex-info \"dao.jing.mem: content address does not match the bytes\"\n    40\t                    {:address address}))))\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\t(defn- put-bytes-fn\n    44\t  \"Backend effect for one byte store: atomic insert-if-absent of a copy of\n    45\t   the bytes. The winner of the CAS returns :inserted; an existing equal\n    46\t   snapshot returns :present; an existing unequal snapshot is a collision\n    47\t   and throws. The closed check happens inside the loop so the operation is\n    48\t   linearizable against close.\"\n    49\t  [state]\n    50\t  (fn [address bs]\n    51\t    (validate-address-bytes! address bs)\n    52\t    (let [snapshot (cbor/copy-bytes bs)]\n    53\t      (loop []\n    54\t        (let [s @state\n    55\t              content (:content s)]\n    56\t          (when (:closed? s)\n    57\t            (throw (ex-info \"dao.jing.mem: content store is closed\"\n    58\t                            {:address address})))\n    59\t          (if (contains? content address)\n    60\t            (if (cbor/bytes= (get content address) bs)\n    61\t              :present\n    62\t              (throw\n    63\t                (ex-info\n    64\t                  (str \"dao.jing.mem: content collision: unequal bytes \"\n    65\t                       \"at the same content address\")\n    66\t                  {:address address})))\n    67\t            (if (compare-and-set! state\n    68\t                                  s\n    69\t                                  (assoc s :content\n    70\t                                         (assoc content address snapshot)))\n    71\t              :inserted\n    72\t              (recur))))))))\n    73\t\n    74\t\n    75\t(defn- get-bytes-fn\n    76\t  \"Backend effect for one byte store: lookup with a caller-supplied\n    77\t   not-found, answering a fresh copy of the stored bytes so the snapshot\n    78\t   stays immutable.\"\n    79\t  [state]\n    80\t  (fn [address not-found]\n    81\t    (let [{:keys [closed? content]} @state]\n    82\t      (when closed?\n    83\t        (throw (ex-info \"dao.jing.mem: content store is closed\"\n    84\t                        {:address address})))\n    85\t      (if (contains? content address)\n    86\t        (cbor/copy-bytes (get content address))\n    87\t        not-found))))\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(defn- close-fn\n    91\t  \"Backend effect for one byte store: idempotent close that returns nil.\"\n    92\t  [state]\n    93\t  (fn [] (swap! state assoc :closed? true) nil))\n    94\t\n    95\t\n    96\t(defn- entries-fn\n    97\t  \"The test-facing snapshot: a map of content address to a fresh copy of\n    98\t   the stored bytes, readable after close.\"\n    99\t  [state]\n   100\t  (fn []\n   101\t    (into {}\n   102\t          (map (fn [[address bs]] [address (cbor/copy-bytes bs)]))\n   103\t          (:content @state))))\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\t(defn create-content-mem\n   107\t  \"Create an ephemeral, thread-safe, content-addressed in-memory DaoJing\n   108\t   byte store.\n   109\t\n   110\t   Returns plain data:\n   111\t\n   112\t     {:put-bytes-fn f\n   113\t      :get-bytes-fn g\n   114\t      :close-fn c\n   115\t      :entries-fn e}\n   116\t\n   117\t   The private state is closed over by the four effects and reachable\n   118\t   through nothing else. The content it holds maps content addresses to\n   119\t   copies of the canonical payload bytes stored at them and never carries a\n   120\t   source stream or provenance stamp.\n   121\t\n   122\t   The optional seed is a map of address to bytes planted verbatim (copied)\n   123\t   and unverified: a test's way to seat forged content behind an address,\n   124\t   which no put could ever do.\"\n   125\t  ([] (create-content-mem {}))\n   126\t  ([seed]\n   127\t   (let [state (atom {:closed? false,\n   128\t                      :content (into {}\n   129\t                                     (map (fn [[address bs]]\n   130\t                                            [address (cbor/copy-bytes bs)]))\n   131\t                                     seed)})]\n   132\t     {:put-bytes-fn (put-bytes-fn state),\n   133\t      :get-bytes-fn (get-bytes-fn state),\n   134\t      :close-fn (close-fn state),\n   135\t      :entries-fn (entries-fn state)})))\n   136\t\n   137\t\n   138\t(defn entries\n   139\t  \"The stored address->value entries of one byte store, each snapshot\n   140\t   hash-verified against its address and decoded -- this backend's\n   141\t   test-facing content view. Seeded bytes that do not hash to their address\n   142\t   make this throw, as any read of them would.\"\n   143\t  [handle]\n   144\t  (into {}\n   145\t        (map (fn [[address bs]] [address (jing/segment-value address bs)]))\n   146\t        ((:entries-fn handle))))\n   147\t\n   148\t\n   149\t(defn entry-bytes\n   150\t  \"The stored address->bytes snapshot of one byte store: fresh copies,\n   151\t   unverified and undecoded, for tests that inspect what a backend holds.\"\n   152\t  [handle]\n   153\t  ((:entries-fn handle)))\n    94\t\n    95\t(def ^:private max-frame-length\n    96\t  \"The largest frame the signed 32-bit length prefix can describe.\"\n    97\t  2147483647)\n    98\t\n    99\t\n   100\t(defn- frame-bytes\n   101\t  \"The frame (without its length prefix) carrying payload bytes at address.\"\n   102\t  [address payload-bytes]\n   103\t  (let [frame (cbor/encode [(hex->bytes (jing/segment-digest address))\n   104\t                            payload-bytes])]\n   105\t    (when (> (byte-count frame) max-frame-length)\n   106\t      (throw (ex-info \"Frame exceeds the length prefix's positive range\"\n   107\t                      {:address address, :length (byte-count frame)})))\n   108\t    frame))\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\t(defn encode-record\n   112\t  \"Encode an [address payload] pair into frame bytes (the length prefix is\n   113\t   written by the frame layer). The payload must hash to the address.\"\n   114\t  [address payload]\n   115\t  (frame-bytes address (jing/segment-bytes address payload)))\n   116\t\n   117\t\n   118\t(defn- decode-frame\n   119\t  \"[address payload-bytes] of one frame: the frame must be exactly one\n   120\t   canonical two-element CBOR array of byte strings, the digest must be\n   121\t   the payload's under some registered algorithm (which then names the\n   122\t   address), and the payload must itself be a canonical Jing payload.\"\n   123\t  [frame]\n   124\t  (let [v (try (cbor/decode frame)\n   125\t               (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   126\t                 (throw (ex-info \"Frame is not a canonical CBOR record\"\n   127\t                                 {:frame frame} e))))]\n   128\t    (when-not (and (vector? v) (= 2 (count v))\n   129\t                   (every? cbor/byte-payload? v))\n   130\t      (throw (ex-info \"Frame is not a [digest payload] array of byte strings\"\n   131\t                      {:record v})))\n   132\t    (let [[digest payload] v\n   133\t          hex (bytes->hex digest)\n   134\t          address-id\n   135\t          (some (fn [[algorithm {:keys [address-id digest-bytes]}]]\n   136\t                  (when (and (= digest-bytes (byte-count digest))\n   137\t                             (= hex (jing/digest-bytes algorithm payload)))\n   138\t                    address-id))\n   139\t                (sort-by key jing/registry))]\n   140\t      (when-not address-id\n   141\t        (throw (ex-info\n   142\t                 (str \"Frame digest is not the payload's under any \"\n   143\t                      \"registered algorithm\")\n   144\t                 {:digest hex})))\n   145\t      (try (cbor/decode payload)\n   146\t           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   147\t             (throw (ex-info \"Frame payload is not a canonical Jing payload\"\n   148\t                             {:digest hex} e))))\n   149\t      [(keyword \"segment\" (str address-id \"-\" hex)) payload])))\n   150\t\n   151\t\n   152\t;; =============================================================================\n   153\t;; Host file primitives -- the only host-aware code below\n   154\t;; =============================================================================\n   155\t\n   156\t(def ^:private prefix-size 4)\n   157\t\n   158\t\n   260\t\n   261\t\n   262\t;; =============================================================================\n   263\t;; Validate-then-truncate replay (F3, F2, F4)\n   264\t;; =============================================================================\n   265\t\n   266\t(defn- torn-tail-offset\n   267\t  \"The offset of the first incomplete frame, scanning from 0: a tail shorter\n   268\t   than the length prefix, a negative length, or a length reaching past\n   269\t   `end` is torn. Returns `end` when every frame is complete.\"\n   270\t  [f end]\n   271\t  (loop [offset 0]\n   272\t    (cond\n   273\t      (>= offset end) end\n   274\t      (< (- end offset) prefix-size) offset\n   275\t      :else (let [len (read-int! f offset)]\n   276\t              (if (or (neg? len) (> (+ offset prefix-size len) end))\n   277\t                offset\n   278\t                (recur (+ offset prefix-size len)))))))\n   279\t\n   280\t\n   281\t(defn- recover!\n   282\t  \"Every complete frame of the file, decoded and validated in order as\n   283\t   [address payload-bytes], with the incomplete tail truncated afterwards.\n   284\t   Validation precedes mutation: a corrupt complete frame, or a nonempty\n   285\t   file with no valid first frame, throws with the file untouched.\"\n   286\t  [f]\n   287\t  (let [end (file-length! f)\n   288\t        cut (torn-tail-offset f end)\n   289\t        records (loop [offset 0, acc []]\n   290\t                  (if (>= offset cut)\n   291\t                    acc\n   292\t                    (let [len (read-int! f offset)]\n   293\t                      (recur (+ offset prefix-size len)\n   294\t                             (conj acc\n   295\t                                   (decode-frame\n   296\t                                     (read-bytes! f (+ offset prefix-size)\n   297\t                                                  len)))))))]\n   298\t    (when (and (pos? end) (empty? records))\n   299\t      (throw (ex-info \"Not a content log: no valid first frame\"\n   300\t                      {:length end})))\n   301\t    (when (< cut end) (truncate-file! f cut))\n   302\t    records))\n   303\t\n   304\t\n   305\t(defn- replay-records\n   306\t  \"Accumulate validated records into the content map. An equal duplicate\n   307\t   record is tolerated (F2), which requires comparing the incoming bytes\n   308\t   with the stored ones; the unequal arm of that comparison fails the open.\n   309\t\n   310\t   That arm is unreachable twice over: decode-frame has already enforced\n   311\t   that a frame's digest hashes its payload, so two validated frames at one\n   312\t   address carry equal bytes; and reaching it otherwise would take a hash\n   313\t   collision, which is not a case to design for. It is retained not as\n   314\t   defence but because F2's tolerate-equal rule forces the comparison, and\n   315\t   the only alternatives to throwing here are to overwrite silently or to\n   316\t   ignore silently -- both of which break `materialize!`'s promise that\n   317\t   nothing is ever overwritten.\"\n   318\t  [records]\n   319\t  (reduce (fn [content [address payload]]\n   320\t            (if (contains? content address)\n   321\t              (if (cbor/bytes= (clojure.core/get content address) payload)\n   322\t                content\n   323\t                (throw (ex-info\n   324\t                         \"Collision: address already holds a different payload\"\n   325\t                         {:address address})))\n   326\t              (assoc content address payload)))\n   327\t          {}\n   328\t          records))\n   329\t\n   330\t\n   331\t;; =============================================================================\n   332\t;; Handle functions (D1, D3, F1)\n   333\t;; =============================================================================\n   334\t\n   335\t(defn- with-lock\n   336\t  #_{:clj-kondo/ignore [:unused-binding]}\n   337\t  [lock f]\n   338\t  #?(:clj (locking lock (f))\n   339\t     :default (f)))\n   340\t\n   341\t\n   342\t(defn- make-put\n   343\t  [state f lock]\n   344\t  (fn content-put!\n   345\t    [address bs]\n   346\t    (when-not (jing/segment-address? address)\n   347\t      (throw (ex-info \"Not a segment content address\" {:address address})))\n   348\t    (when-not (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bs)\n   349\t      (throw (ex-info \"Segment address does not match the bytes\"\n   350\t                      {:address address})))\n   351\t    (let [snapshot (cbor/copy-bytes bs)\n   352\t          frame (frame-bytes address snapshot)]\n   353\t      (with-lock\n   354\t        lock\n   355\t        (fn []\n   356\t          (let [{:keys [closed? content]} @state]\n   357\t            (when closed?\n   358\t              (throw (ex-info \"Content file is closed\" {:address address})))\n   359\t            (if (contains? content address)\n   360\t              (if (cbor/bytes= (clojure.core/get content address) bs)\n   361\t                :present\n   362\t                (throw (ex-info\n   363\t                         \"Collision: address already holds a different payload\"\n   364\t                         {:address address})))\n   365\t              (do\n   366\t                (append-frame! f frame)\n   367\t                (sync-file! f)\n   368\t                (swap! state assoc-in [:content address] snapshot)\n   369\t                :inserted))))))))\n   370\t\n   371\t\n   372\t(defn- make-get\n   373\t  [state]\n   374\t  (fn content-get\n   375\t    [address not-found]\n   376\t    (let [{:keys [closed? content]} @state]\n   377\t      (when closed?\n   378\t        (throw (ex-info \"Content file is closed\" {:address address})))\n   379\t      (if (contains? content address)\n   380\t        (cbor/copy-bytes (clojure.core/get content address))\n   381\t        not-found))))\n   382\t\n   383\t\n   384\t(defn- make-close\n   385\t  [state f lock]\n   284\t                                       (canonical-class (val entry))))\n   285\t                                v))\n   286\t               :map)\n   287\t    (set? v) (when (every? canonical-class v) :set)\n   288\t    (vector? v) (when (every? canonical-class v) :vector)\n   289\t    (sequential? v) (when (every? canonical-class v) :list)\n   290\t    (number? v) (numeric-class v)))\n   291\t\n   292\t\n   293\t(defn canonical-value?\n   294\t  \"True when `v` is inside §5's canonical value domain — equivalently,\n   295\t   when `canonical-class` is non-nil.\"\n   296\t  [v]\n   297\t  (some? (canonical-class v)))\n   298\t\n   299\t\n   300\t(defn normalize-nfc\n   301\t  \"The one NFC seam of the projection (§5): every string entering\n   302\t   canonical encoding passes through here. :clj delegates to\n   303\t   java.text.Normalizer, :cljs to String.prototype.normalize, and :cljd\n   304\t   to the unorm_dart package (Unicode 16.0, owner-settled 2026-09-21) so\n   305\t   every ClojureDart target normalizes identically. NFC normalisation\n   306\t   collisions — distinct inputs with one composed form — are an\n   307\t   inherited limit of the repository encoding.\"\n   308\t  [^String s]\n   309\t  #?(:clj (java.text.Normalizer/normalize s java.text.Normalizer$Form/NFC)\n   310\t     :cljs (.normalize s \"NFC\")\n   311\t     :cljd (unorm/nfc s)))\n   312\t\n  1160\t\n  1161\t\n  1162\t(def ^:private record-attributes\n  1163\t  \"Every attribute a projected record entity may carry: the declared\n  1164\t   dimension slots, markers included.\"\n  1165\t  (into #{} (map first) dimension-slots))\n  1166\t\n  1167\t\n  1168\t(defn- slot-shape-ok?\n  1169\t  \"Whether `v` fits the descriptor `type` on a projected record: the\n  1170\t   deterministic gate the storage reader hashes behind, so a wrongly\n  1171\t   typed slot — :yin.debruijn/bound 5, a numeric child ref — diagnoses\n  1172\t   :unsupported-value instead of reaching host arithmetic inside the\n  1173\t   hash recomputation.\"\n  1174\t  [type v]\n  1175\t  (cond\n  1176\t    (= :canonical type) (canonical-value? v)\n  1177\t    (= :keyword type) (keyword? v)\n  1178\t    (= :symbol type) (symbol? v)\n  1179\t    (= :string type) (string? v)\n  1180\t    (= :bool type) (or (true? v) (false? v))\n  1181\t    (= :int64 type) (and (number? v) (= :int64 (numeric-class v)))\n  1182\t    (or (= :ref type) (= :hash type)) (and (string? v)\n  1183\t                                           (re-matches #\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\" v))\n   485\t        (lit 1.5)\n   486\t        (lit :ns/kw)\n   487\t        (lit 'ns/sym)\n   488\t        (lit [1 \"a\" :k])\n   489\t        (lit #{1 \"b\" :c})\n   490\t        (lit {:a [1 2], \"k\" #{nil}}))])\n   491\t\n   492\t\n   493\t(deftest every-node-type-and-scalar-class-round-trips-through-durable-storage\n   494\t  (let [path (temp-path)]\n   495\t    (try\n   496\t      (let [store (jing-file/create-content-file path)\n   497\t            addresses (mapv (fn [ast]\n   498\t                              (get-in (persist! ast (recording-writer) store)\n   499\t                                      [:projected :address]))\n   500\t                            durable-programs)\n   501\t            _ (jing/close! store)\n   502\t            reopened (jing-file/create-content-file path)\n   503\t            stored (mapv (fn [address]\n   504\t                           (:yin.debruijn/datoms (jing/get reopened address ::absent)))\n   505\t                         addresses)]\n   506\t        (jing/close! reopened)\n   507\t        (is (every? jing/segment-address? addresses))\n   508\t        (doseq [[ast datoms] (map vector durable-programs stored)]\n   509\t          (is (= (select-keys (debruijn/project-datoms\n   510\t                                (second (vm/ast->datoms-with-root ast)))\n   511\t                              [:fingerprint :records])\n   512\t                 (debruijn/datoms->projected datoms))\n   513\t              \"the reopened envelope reads back to the original projection\")))\n   514\t      (finally (cleanup-file path)))))\n   515\t\n   516\t\n   517\t(def ^:private host\n   567\t              (when (= :ok (:outcome projected))\n   568\t                (is (= original\n   569\t                       (let [reopened (jing-file/create-content-file path)\n   570\t                             stored (:yin.debruijn/datoms\n   571\t                                      (jing/get reopened (:address projected) ::absent))]\n   572\t                         (jing/close! reopened)\n   573\t                         (debruijn/datoms->projected stored)))\n   574\t                    \"hosts already shown to carry the value carry it exactly\"))))\n   575\t          (finally (cleanup-file path)))))))\n   576\t\n   577\t\n   578\t(deftest list-literals-persist-in-memory\n   579\t  ;; the durable file codec does not carry lists on every host; the\n   580\t  ;; pipeline itself does, and keeps a list distinct from a vector\n   581\t  (let [store (mem-store)\n   582\t        as-list (persist! (app (v 'list) (lit (list 1 2.5))) (recording-writer) store)\n   583\t        as-vector (persist! (app (v 'list) (lit [1 2.5])) (recording-writer) store)]\n   584\t    (is (= :ok (:outcome (:projected as-list)) (:outcome (:projected as-vector))))\n   585\t    (is (= {:yin.debruijn/fingerprint (get-in as-list [:projected :fingerprint]),\n   586\t            :yin.debruijn/datoms (debruijn/projected->datoms\n   587\t                                   (debruijn/project-datoms\n   588\t                                     (second (vm/ast->datoms-with-root\n   589\t                                               (app (v 'list) (lit (list 1 2.5)))))))}\n   590\t           (jing/get store (get-in as-list [:projected :address]) ::absent)))\n   591\t    (is (not= (get-in as-list [:projected :fingerprint])\n   592\t              (get-in as-vector [:projected :fingerprint])))))\n   593\t\n   594\t\n   595\t(deftest renamed-programs-store-equal-projected-datoms\n   527\t  Dart producer must clear constructor metadata itself\n   528\t  (`(with-meta (apply list xs) nil)`) before handing a payload to\n   529\t  `dao.jing`; decoded lists carry none. This obligation carries forward\n   530\t  unchanged from `dao.jing.cbor.md`.\n   531\t- **The intake transport's portable domain is narrower than Jing's.** The\n   532\t  `dao.stream` Transit codec carries no metadata, byte strings, or rich\n   533\t  numerics, so such payloads reach Jing only through direct `materialize!`\n   534\t  calls; the intake fail-closed rule carries forward unchanged.\n   535\t- **Decoded numeric carriers on JavaScript.** Floating-point, decimal, and\n   536\t  rational content decode to Jing's portable carriers on JavaScript, never\n   537\t  to a bare number; a consumer that reads values back from a store and\n   538\t  pattern-matches on host number types (today, `yin.vm.debruijn`'s slot\n   539\t  type check) must accept the carriers, per `dao.jing.cbor.md`'s numeric\n   540\t  identity section.\n   541\t- **Durable observer checkpoints / long-running runner.** `observer-state`\n   542\t  and `observe-step!` are single-step and in-process. The checkpoint records,\n   543\t  per member, the stream coordinate plus the transport-minted cursor; the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
