{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/resources/dao/jing/digest-table.edn | sed -n '24,38p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/data/btree/storage.cljc | sed -n '1,33p'; nl -ba docs/design/dao.jing.hash-registry.md | sed -n '500,528p'; git diff --name-only -- src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc; git diff --unified=0 -- test/yin/vm/pipeline_test.cljc | sed -n '1,90p'; rg -n 'copy-bytes|byte-payload\\\\?|defn bytes=' src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc | head -18\"","aggregated_output":"    24\t;; fixture readers agree on what bytes to feed their provider before any\n    25\t;; comparison happens. A hex string too long for one line is written as a\n    26\t;; vector of string chunks, concatenated by the reader.\n    27\t;;\n    28\t;; Canonical-Clojure-data-structure cases were produced by hashing the\n    29\t;; exact bytes `dao.jing/canonical-bytes` returns for the given value:\n    30\t;; the canonical CBOR payload of docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md, as\n    31\t;; `dao.jing.cbor/encode` writes it (the clean break from the earlier\n    32\t;; order-normalized print encoder; regenerated 2026-09-24 along with every\n    33\t;; other DaoJing address fixture, per that plan's clean-break ruling).\n    34\t\n    35\t{:providers {:jvm  \"io.github.rctcwyvrn/blake3 1.3\"\n    36\t             :cljs \"@noble/hashes 2.4.0\"\n    37\t             :cljd \"blake3_dart 1.0.0\"}\n    38\t\n     1\t(ns dao.data.btree.storage\n     2\t  \"IStorage adapters over dao.jing content-store handles (docs/design/dao.data.btree.md\n     3\t   §5.1, §5.4). A handle is the plain-data byte store carrying\n     4\t   :put-bytes-fn, :get-bytes-fn, and :close-fn (docs/design/dao.jing.md,\n     5\t   Materialization rule); addresses are derived from payloads by\n     6\t   dao.jing/materialize!, never supplied by this layer. Two adapters, one\n     7\t   error taxonomy:\n     8\t\n     9\t   - KVStorage (kv-storage): the sync rule-1 adapter. Absence is\n    10\t     authoritative: a missing blob throws \\\"missing index segment\\\".\n    11\t     Optional same-host integrity verification (§5.2): rehash the fetched\n    12\t     blob against its content address; mismatch throws \\\"corrupt index\n    13\t     segment\\\". Off by default — dao.jing's print-based content hash is not\n    14\t     host-stable, so cross-host reads must not verify (dao.jing.md, Current\n    15\t     Scope).\n    16\t   - HydrationStorage (hydration-storage): the §5.4 hydration-cache\n    17\t     adapter for async-only backends. Reads answer only from the cache;\n    18\t     any miss throws \\\"unhydrated segment\\\" — the cache cannot distinguish\n    19\t     absent from not-yet-fetched without blocking on the backend. hydrate!\n    20\t     copies the reachable blob graph from the source into the cache. The\n    21\t     source is either a sync content handle or an async one\n    22\t     (dao.jing.remote.async/async-content); over an async source the\n    23\t     non-blocking hydrate-async and store-tree-async are the only way in\n    24\t     and out, and the sync store path throws.\n    25\t\n    26\t   dao.data.btree itself stays storage-agnostic; this namespace is the one\n    27\t   place the tree meets dao.jing (Decision 1: no new storage protocol —\n    28\t   everything below is materialize!/get, plus segment-matches? for §5.2\n    29\t   verification).\"\n    30\t  (:require #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:async\" :as async]])\n    31\t            [dao.data.btree :as bt]\n    32\t            [dao.jing :as jing]))\n    33\t\n   500\t\n   501\tAny provider version or replacement that changes a pinned digest is rejected as nonconforming to the registered algorithm.\n   502\t\n   503\t## Sequencing with canonical CBOR\n   504\t\n   505\tThe algorithm-registry epic lands first over the current order-normalized print encoder.\n   506\t\n   507\tIt establishes:\n   508\t\n   509\t- the flat multihash address grammar;\n   510\t- permanent BLAKE3 and SHA-256 entries;\n   511\t- BLAKE3 as the minting default;\n   512\t- explicit SHA-256 minting;\n   513\t- algorithm-directed verification; and\n   514\t- algorithm-preserving copy paths.\n   515\t\n   516\tCanonical CBOR remains a separate clean-break epic. A canonical codec already exists in `dao.jing.cbor`; its byte contract is frozen by `test/resources/dao/jing/cbor-v1.json` and is currently used for encoded comparison rather than addressing.\n   517\t\n   518\tWhen CBOR lands, it replaces the implementation of `canonical-bytes` outright. The algorithm registry remains unchanged:\n   519\t\n   520\t- BLAKE3 remains the default;\n   521\t- SHA-256 remains explicitly selectable;\n   522\t- the address grammar remains `:segment/<algorithm-id>-<digest>`;\n   523\t- every digest and every DaoJing address is regenerated from CBOR bytes;\n   524\t- development stores, fixtures, manifests, ASTs, and continuations are rebuilt together; and\n   525\t- no printer-address reader, alias, graph migration, or encoding negotiation is introduced.\n   526\t\n   527\tThe existing `dao.jing.cbor.md` \"Addressing and clean break\" ruling remains authoritative. This document changes its SHA-only algorithm assumption but does not alter its clean-break policy.\n   528\t\ndiff --git a/test/yin/vm/pipeline_test.cljc b/test/yin/vm/pipeline_test.cljc\nindex f125db49..88d5fc29 100644\n--- a/test/yin/vm/pipeline_test.cljc\n+++ b/test/yin/vm/pipeline_test.cljc\n@@ -82,12 +82,12 @@\n-            :put-content-fn (fn [address payload]\n-                              (let [result (if (contains? @store address)\n-                                             :present\n-                                             (do (swap! store assoc address payload)\n-                                                 :inserted))]\n-                                (note! [:put address result])\n-                                result))\n-            :get-content-fn (fn [address not-found]\n-                              (note! [:get address])\n-                              (if (contains? @store address)\n-                                (get @store address)\n-                                not-found))))))\n+            :put-bytes-fn (fn [address bs]\n+                            (let [result (if (contains? @store address)\n+                                           :present\n+                                           (do (swap! store assoc address bs)\n+                                               :inserted))]\n+                              (note! [:put address result])\n+                              result))\n+            :get-bytes-fn (fn [address not-found]\n+                            (note! [:get address])\n+                            (if (contains? @store address)\n+                              (get @store address)\n+                              not-found))))))\n@@ -100,2 +100,2 @@\n-  {:put-content-fn (fn [_address _payload] :not-a-result),\n-   :get-content-fn (fn [_address not-found] not-found)})\n+  {:put-bytes-fn (fn [_address _bytes] :not-a-result),\n+   :get-bytes-fn (fn [_address not-found] not-found)})\n@@ -115 +115,4 @@\n-                              @backing)))))\n+                              (into {}\n+                                    (map (fn [[a bs]]\n+                                           [a (jing/segment-value a bs)]))\n+                                    @backing))))))\n308:(defn bytes=\n767:    (wire/byte-payload? x) (hash (bytes-hex x))\n790:    (or (wire/byte-payload? a) (wire/byte-payload? b))\n791:    (and (wire/byte-payload? a) (wire/byte-payload? b) (bytes= a b))\n884:    (wire/byte-payload? x) [::bytes (bytes-hex x)]\n1114:    (wire/byte-payload? x) (do (deep! d :unsupported-value)\n1137:(defn byte-payload?\n1141:  (wire/byte-payload? x))\n1144:(defn copy-bytes\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
